; fas9_material_styles.scr - facit for step 9.7 (MATERIAL, the VISUALSTYLE forms and what uses them; F9.6, F9.7). Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_material_styles.scr --input doc/facit/acad_2018_dxf_native_records.dxf
; (AutoCAD 2025's core; the input is AutoCAD's own DXF from 21_native_records.scr, which has the material HDXF_SIX_MAPS with all
; six maps and non-identity mapper transforms and the standard materials ByBlock, ByLayer and Global). Plain AutoCAD commands, no
; LISP; see fas9_example.scr.
;
; The core has no command that makes or edits a material (-MATERIALS, MATERIALATTACH, MATERIALMAP, MATBROWSEROPEN, -RMAT and
; MATERIALASSIGN are "Unknown command" in V.72.0.0): the material comes in with the input drawing, and the core attaches it
; (-LAYER MATerial, CHPROP Material) and purges it (-PURGE MAterials). A change of a material's channel or procedure needs the GUI:
; the pair doc/facit/acad_*_dxf_native_records_material_changed.dxf (21_native_records.scr) is the only one (plan 9.7, "Ej testat",
; F9.6: procedural materials, the 2007 normal map and the modern channels have no AutoCAD file at all).
;
; Visual styles: the system variables VSFACESTYLE ... VSSHADOWS change the current style and -VISUALSTYLES Saveas keeps the result
; under a name; one style is made with the face settings, one with the edge settings, one with the display settings; Current puts one
; in the model space viewport (VPORT 348) and in a saved view (VIEW 348); Rename and Delete follow. One style is current in a layout
; viewport (VIEWPORT 348). The core has no screen, so a viewport is made with MVIEW and made current with MSPACE.
;
; Not made here (no command in the core; plan 9.7, "Ej testat"): a visual style on an entity of its own (full, face and edge
; style, the 349/350 groups: no AutoCAD file has them; 348 is the VIEWPORT's, VPORT's and VIEW's), SUNSTUDY, a material with a
; procedure or a normal map, a channel changed by the program.
